other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianInglis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-28T09:07:21Z","updated_at":"2023-08-28T09:07:21Z","body":"Looks like typos in the original, which should be patched to correct, as the conditions and warranties may be considered to not have been properly disclaimed: \r\n\r\n> The MPEG Software Simulation Group disclaims any and all warranties, \r\nwhether express, implied, or ~statuary,~ **statutory,** including any implied warranties ~or~ **of** merchantability or of fitness for a particular purpose. \r\n\r\n[Implied warranty: Merchantability](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Implied_warranty#Merchantability)\r\n\r\nDoes that mean MPEG statuary grants warranties on this software? \r\n[ISO and IEC expert group wins another Emmy Award: MPEG file format subgroup recognized for essential contribution to video and audio technology](https://www.iso.org/news/ref2741.html) and \r\n[Record-breaking MPEG takes two Emmy Awards: Two new Emmys go to IEC and ISO for their ground-breaking MPEG standards](https://www.iso.org/contents/news/2022/04/record-breaking-mpeg-takes-two-e.html) \r\n ;^> ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1695321903/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-X